<p><strong>Product</strong>: <a href="https://www.ia.net/writer" target="_blank">iA Writer</a><br>
<strong>Price</strong>: $49.99</p>
<h2 id="ia-writer-8-growing-up-with-care">iA Writer 8 Growing Up With Care</h2>
<p>Major versions of iA Writer include a critical feature or two. The developers do not make huge changes to the program. They are deliberate about the changes/additions they make.</p>
<h2 id="uniting-search-and-navigation">Uniting Search and Navigation</h2>
<p><img src="https://cdn.blot.im/blog_c4a729f3205a44e5a9669523ddfb8b2e/_image_cache/0b5fdebe-9acf-49b5-9c38-a977bb2bfa05/ia8a.png" alt="Search and Navigation (⇧⌘O)" width="397" height="337" data-action="zoom"><span class="caption">Search and Navigation (⇧⌘O)</span></p>
<p>The most important feature of iA Writer 8 is the new search and navigation palette. It’s so simple and yet so powerful. All the headings in your document are shown. Pick one, hit ↵ and you navigate to it. In the case of a long document, this is a great feature.</p>
<p><img src="https://cdn.blot.im/blog_c4a729f3205a44e5a9669523ddfb8b2e/_image_cache/8d3a1bc4-6be3-407f-bf99-02326af5bd66/ia8b.png" alt="Search and Navigation in Your Library" width="402" height="675" data-action="zoom"><span class="caption">Search and Navigation in Your Library</span></p>
<p>You press <code>⇧⌘O</code> to open quick search palette. Type what you are looking for and it looks for the content in the document and in the files in your library.</p>
<h2 id="command-palette">Command Palette</h2>
<p><img src="https://cdn.blot.im/blog_c4a729f3205a44e5a9669523ddfb8b2e/_image_cache/c81c28e5-8c93-4c24-9a69-565bd9095599/ia8c.png" alt="Command Palette (⇧⌘P)" width="388" height="138" data-action="zoom"><span class="caption">Command Palette (⇧⌘P)</span></p>
<p>This is a feature which is shared by many other text editors. You press <code>⇧⌘P</code> and you get a pop-up. Type the command you are looking for, it is shown in the palette. Hit return and you execute the command. I remember seeing this in Sublime Text years ago, iA Writer has this now. It is useful. The good news is that the keyboard command is also shown next to the command. Nice way of learning the keyboard command, and if you use that, you don’t need to invoke the command palette at all.</p>
<p>This is a good feature designed to make life comfortable for newbies to iA Writer.</p>
<h2 id="liquid-glass">Liquid Glass</h2>
<p>I am not excited about this. iA Writer has always been minimal and beautiful to look at. They have added some Liquid Glass touches and it makes iA Writer look better. Or at least conform to Tahoe. Since there is very little extraneous chrome around iA Writer it is a negligible change at best.</p>
<h2 id="authorship-menus">Authorship Menus</h2>
<p>Not something I care about. I don’t use AI for writing, and I am doing all of my writing myself. Must be useful if you do use AI and also if there are multiple people working on the same document.</p>
<h2 id="changes-to-the-sidebar">Changes to the Sidebar</h2>
<p>These are little changes which make the overall feel of the program better. Tiny UI changes and the tweaked display of information in the chrome of the application.</p>
<h2 id="overall-feel-of-writing-in-the-app">Overall Feel of Writing in the App</h2>
<p>iA Writer has always been a pleasure to write in. That has been a constant over all the versions of this application. Of all the Markdown based text editors in the marketplace (and there are so many of them), iA Writer is the one I keep coming back to. It is the best Markdown based text editor in the marketplace. That hasn’t changed.</p>
<h2 id="conclusion">Conclusion</h2>
<p>If you are looking for a Markdown based text editor, you cannot go wrong with iA Writer. It is developed by people who sweat the details, they add features and tweaks with care and reason. I love writing in iA Writer.</p>
<p>I recommend iA Writer heartily.</p>
